.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=DskTools


@Contents
$ #DskTools#
 Browses and edits disk images of retro computers: Agat and Apple II
(DOS 3.3, ProDOS, Sprite OS, Onix), CP/M machines (Korvet, Orion,
Vector, Irisha...), MS-DOS and Atari ST diskettes (FAT), DVK, BK and
UKNC (RT-11), Iskra-226. Raw sector images, HFE, MFM/NIB/NIC, AIM, IMD.
 Files can be written into raw sector images with CP/M, DOS 3.3, FAT
and RT-11; the image file is saved right after every operation.

 #Opening an image#
 Open the disk image under the cursor             #Enter, Ctrl+PgDn#
 Open an image from the command line                    #dsk:<file>#
 Close the image (at its root)              #Enter on .., Ctrl+PgUp#

 #Inside the image#
 Copy, move to the other panel or into the image            #F5, F6#
 Copy under another name in the same folder               #Shift+F5#
 Rename                                                   #Shift+F6#
 Make a folder (CP/M: a user area)                              #F7#
 Delete                                                         #F8#
 View, edit                                                 #F3, F4#
 Information about the image                                #Ctrl+L#
 Find files                                                 #Alt+F7#

 CP/M user areas 1..31 are shown as folders #USER_01#..#USER_31#. #F6# between
two panels of one CP/M image moves the files into the other user area.
